# Automatic differentiation

The `math/grad` package computes derivatives of GX functions.

`grad.Reverse(square)` returns a new function generated by the compiler. That function returns the result of `square` together with a backward function. The backward function computes a vector-Jacobian product: called with 1, it returns the derivative of `square` at 3, that is, 6. In the implementation of `vjp` (output by `trace(vjp)`), note the use of a closure to store intermediate results of the forward pass and to reuse them in the backward pass.

When a function has several arguments, like `linear`, `grad.Reverse` returns one backward function per argument. Each gradient has the same type as its argument.

